      "overview": "The lesson focused on the methodology and arrangement of topics in the classical Ḥanafī work Uṣūl al-Shāshī. The instructor explained that one of the distinguishing characteristics of this text is its unique arrangement of discussions compared to other classical Ḥanafī uṣūl works such as Manār al-Anwār. Although the author generally follows the traditional Ḥanafī framework of categorization, he rearranges several discussions and omits others for the sake of brevity.\nThe traditional Ḥanafī method commonly divides the discussions related to the Qurʾān into four major categories known as Wujūh al-Kalām or Wujūh al-Naẓar fī al-Alfāẓ. These are:\nوُجُوهُ الْوَضْعِ (Wujūh al-Waḍʿ)\nوُجُوهُ الْبَيَانِ (Wujūh al-Bayān)\nوُجُوهُ الِاسْتِعْمَالِ (Wujūh al-Istiʿmāl)\nوُجُوهُ الِاسْتِدْلَالِ (Wujūh al-Istidlāl)\nThese categories represent different ways in which legal theorists study language and derive rulings from revelation.\nWujūh al-Waḍʿ concerns how words are originally assigned meanings. Wujūh al-Bayān studies the clarity and ambiguity of expressions. Wujūh al-Istiʿmāl examines how language is used literally and figuratively. Wujūh al-Istidlāl discusses how meanings and rulings are extracted from textual evidence.\nThe author of Uṣūl al-Shāshī generally follows this structure but rearranges the sequence in a manner different from many standard Ḥanafī manuals.",
